&lt;p&gt;Hudson River Trading (HRT) is seeking an APAC Tax Specialist to join our growing Tax team. In this role, you&#39;ll help manage income tax workstreams across the Asia-Pacific region and collaborate with teams across the firm on strategic tax planning initiatives. It&#39;s an exciting opportunity to make a meaningful impact and grow your expertise across multiple APAC jurisdictions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare income tax provision and income tax return workpapers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare tax footnotes for audited financial statements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary point of contact for APAC based tax advisors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with external advisors in reviewing and filing income tax returns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a tax compliance calendar and coordinate tax payments for APAC entities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide support in responding to inquiries from tax authorities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze tax treaty issues including treaty applicability and permanent establishments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with transfer pricing compliance obligations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with accounting, finance, and legal teams on projects to create tax efficiencies and improve tax structuring in relation to APAC entities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research tax issues and communicate findings clearly to internal stakeholders&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor legislative and regulatory developments impacting tax in the APAC region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or related field&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years experience in corporate income tax managing tax compliance obligations across multiple jurisdictions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with income tax rules in key APAC markets such as Singapore, Hong Kong, India, Korea, and China preferred; familiarity with additional regional jurisdictions is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to quickly familiarize oneself with the income tax rules of new tax jurisdictions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Excel skills, with the ability to independently read, edit, and create tax workpapers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills, with excellent organizational abilities and meticulous attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional cross-functional written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to multitask and prioritize projects in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, problem-solving, and critical thinking skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Impeccable ethics, integrity, and discretion when working with confidential information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work both independently and within a team, and take initiative to identify and resolve issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s in Taxation or CPA preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public accounting and finance/trading industry experience preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
