&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in data sourcing, market data, broker data, quantitative research data, vendor management, or a related role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of data sources, dataset evaluation, and how data can be used in a quantitative research or systematic trading context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with external counterparties and internal research, legal, business, and technology teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meticulously detail-oriented, with the ability to work independently in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data analysis skills, including proficiency with Python, SQL, or similar tools is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The estimated base salary range for this position is $150,000 - 250,000 per year, based on job-related skills and experience. This role will also be eligible for discretionary performance-based bonuses and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
