&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver people analytics insights and reporting for both leadership and company-wide audiences, translating complex findings into clear, actionable narratives&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build predictive models for projections such as headcount growth and time-to-fill forecasting, and conduct deep-dive investigations into workforce trends&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the design of a single source of truth for people data — defining the data model, schema, and metric requirements — and partner with data engineering to build and maintain a structured, auditable repository that replaces fragmented spreadsheets&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a standardized metrics library (definitions, sources, methodologies, refresh cadences) and maintain automated dashboards that serve self-service needs for People Ops and managers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage, mentor, and develop the People Analytics team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish data governance policies including data access controls, privacy compliance, documentation standards, and quality assurance processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct deep-dive investigations into workforce trends and present findings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with other teams to integrate people data with financial and operational datasets for cross-functional insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set analytics roadmap aligned to People Operations and business strategy, managing competing priorities with a clear intake and prioritization process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive stakeholder engagement by proactively identifying high-value analytics opportunities and building trust through consistent, reliable delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion a culture of data literacy across the People Ops function and broader organisation through training, enablement sessions, and accessible reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s in a quantitative field (e.g., I/O Psychology, Statistics, Data Science, Economics); relevant Master&#39;s or analytics-focused MBA preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of progressive people analytics experience, including 5+ years leading an analytics team and 5+ years embedded within or alongside HR across the full employee lifecycle&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting 1,000+ global or multi-site workforce preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in regression, modeling, clustering, factor analysis, and A/B testing for workforce questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience partnering with data engineers to build a people data warehouse — defining the data model, specifying requirements, and validating delivered data — without needing to build the pipelines yourself&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in SQL and Python or R for analysis, modeling, and prototyping, with enough understanding of data warehousing and ETL/ELT to guide and validate engineering work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to drive AI/LLM solutions for data synthesis and workforce storytelling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL (complex joins, CTEs, window functions) and proficiency in Python/R for statistical modeling and automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and governing a people data warehouse in close partnership with data engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Workday and Workday analytics (Advanced/Matrix Reporting, Calculated Fields, Prism)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Excel/Google Sheets skills for ad-hoc analysis; ability and desire to reduce spreadsheet dependency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with People platforms (Culture Amp, Greenhouse, etc.) and data integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with multi-country data privacy regulations (GDPR, CCPA) preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The estimated base salary range for this position is &lt;em&gt;$225,000-$275,000&lt;/em&gt;, based on job-related skills and experience. This role will also be eligible for discretionary performance-based bonuses and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
