&lt;p&gt;​​&lt;em&gt;The application deadline for this position is &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-rich-links=&quot;{&amp;quot;dat_df&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;fres_frt&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;fres_usd&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;dfie_ts&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;tv&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;tv_s&amp;quot;:1792152000,&amp;quot;tv_n&amp;quot;:0}},&amp;quot;dfie_l&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;en&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;dfie_p&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;fres_frt&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;fres_usd&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;tres_tv&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;MMM d, y&amp;quot;},&amp;quot;dfie_dt&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Oct 16, 2026&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;dfie_pt&amp;quot;:3,&amp;quot;dfie_tpt&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;dfie_tzi&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;},&amp;quot;type&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;date&amp;quot;}&quot;&gt;Oct 30, 2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HRT is seeking qualified PhD candidates for our Winter Internship Program. Our PhD Winter Internship program is a 3 week introduction to quantitative research designed for graduate students with little or no experience in quantitative trading. Over the course of the program, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn about a wide range of trading styles from leading experts in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on independent research projects, representative of real work at HRT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train models on our state of the art compute cluster&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore all that New York City has to offer through a variety of social events and tech talks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This program begins on January 4, 2027. This is an in-person program and will take place in our New York City office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a full-time PhD student graduating between fall 2027 and summer 2029 in a technical or quantitative discipline (math, physics, computer science, statistics, machine learning, or a related program)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience in programming; familiarity with Python and/or C++ is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for technology and excitement for learning something new&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional problem solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This program is specifically offered for individuals without extensive experience in the quantitative trading industry.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
