&lt;p&gt;Hudson River Trading (HRT) is looking for a Treasury Associate to assist with firm-wide capital and liquidity management. The role will involve collaborating with other teams to manage day-to-day capital deployment, FX exposure and hedging, and counterparty risks. In addition, you will coordinate treasury activities to ensure adequate funding throughout the business. Successful candidates will bring an interest in financial technology, capital markets, FX risk management, and process improvement, coupled with the critical thinking skills necessary to optimize capital management and treasury functions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide comprehensive coverage of cash and capital management, including daily cash operations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor regulatory and operational capital, collateral, and liquidity, ensuring optimal capital allocation across clearing firms, brokers, and banking partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze financing costs, balances, and credit facilities to optimize the firm&#39;s funding mix&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate yield and interest rate risks, and execute yield enhancement strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage end-to-end margin workflows across brokers and counterparties, including analyzing and meeting margin requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and execute hedging strategies and transactions to manage multi-currency FX exposure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess, monitor, and report on bank and broker counterparty risk exposure, setting limits and monitoring risk metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manager bank account coordination, and documentation, including opening, maintaining, and closing bank accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee our credit card program, including requests for new cards, limits, and fraudulent transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with software engineering teams and leverage treasury tools to improve analysis and automation, and build globally scalable treasury infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the rollout of new initiatives in cash and capital management, cash forecasting, analysis, reporting, data collection, analytical tool development, process improvement, and automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist senior treasury team members with additional departmental initiatives as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across the broader Finance team to gain visibility into HRT&#39;s financial strategy and drive corporate finance initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in finance, accounting, or a related field&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in Treasury, Capital Markets, Prime Brokerage, or Financial Engineering within a bank, hedge fund, asset manager, or trading firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible, reliable, and conscientious, with keen attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to handle multiple priorities in a time-sensitive and dynamic environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Excel and basic programming skills in any language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please note that this specific role is not currently eligible for visa sponsorship. For roles that are eligible for visa sponsorship, please continue to check our listings!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
